/* book exam traps: Putting mole fractions y and x into an operating line drawn in mole ratios Y and X. Convert with Y = y/(1 − y) and X = x/(1 − x) first. | Using the total liquid flow instead of the solute-free solvent flow L. If the entering solvent already contains solute, L = Ltotal,in(1 − xin), with xin taken at the inlet; using the outlet x understates L. | Mixing the ends: Yout belongs with Xin at the top, and Yin belongs with Xout at the bottom. The intercept is Yout only when Xin = 0. | Reversing the rule for absorption: absorption needs the operating line above the equilibrium line; stripping needs it below. | Treating the driving force as constant along the column. The gap changes from end to end, which is why packed towers use a log mean driving force. */
